      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:alsood'
    'female|a||But a win was only a ticket: a winner still had to send back forms and show an income below the poverty line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:uzaulx'
    female|a||First, a guess. What share of the people drawn were on Medicaid within a year or so? Set the bar to your guess.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:stzxff'
    female|a||About four in ten. Many forms never came back, and about half of those that did failed the income test.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Among those not drawn, about fourteen in a hundred got onto Medicaid anyway, by other routes.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:p3ti28'
    female|a||So winning raised coverage by about twenty-six percentage points. That jump is the lottery's first stage.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ov94t'
    female|a||The tempting next step is to compare the winners who enrolled with the winners who didn't.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:p3j3p4'
    female|a||But enrolling was a choice, and whatever drove it, being sick, being organised, needing care, travels straight into their medical bills.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:s851rl'
    'female|a||The honest comparison keeps the lottery''s own two groups: everyone drawn against everyone not drawn, whatever they did next.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:2aeppb'
    'female|a||To keep the arithmetic in view, take made-up numbers: over six months, the drawn spend a hundred and fifty-five dollars out of pocket, the rest two hundred and thirty-three.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1e9g0sz'
    female|a||So winning cut spending by seventy-eight dollars a head. That gap is the intention-to-treat effect, and it is honest.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12niun5'
    female|a||But it is spread over everyone drawn, when the draw changed coverage for only twenty-six in every hundred.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1p2vymi'
    female|a||So who are those twenty-six, and what did coverage do for them? We'll sort the applicants into types, count the ones who moved, and divide.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:kxfk5i'
    'female|a||Call being on Medicaid D. Before a single name is drawn, every applicant already has two answers: her D if drawn, and her D if not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12160
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Each answer is yes or no, so the two answers sort the applicants into four kinds.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1bvgwm7'
    female|a||Some are on Medicaid either way. These always-takers qualify by another route, such as a disability.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:13fgpi9'
    female|a||Some stay off either way. Never-takers never send the forms back, or turn out to earn too much.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:18ha7yg'
    female|a||And some are on Medicaid only if drawn. These compliers are the only people the lottery actually moves.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:air2km'
    female|a||The last cell would hold defiers, who'd sign up only if they lost. The method assumes this cell is empty, and that assumption is called monotonicity.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1e933hn'
    'female|a||Here it is easy to believe: losing a lottery gives nobody a new reason to enrol.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:iiufr5'
    female|a||Now count them. Because the draw was random, the drawn and the not drawn hold the same mix of the three kinds.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:pyq07j'
    'female|a||Among those not drawn, the ones on Medicaid sit in the left column, and with no defiers that means only always-takers: fourteen in a hundred.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1gr8dgj'
    'female|a||Among those drawn, the ones on Medicaid sit in the top row: always-takers and compliers together, forty in a hundred.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9qyoap'
    female|a||Subtract, and the always-takers cancel. The first stage, twenty-six points, is exactly the share of compliers, and the other sixty are never-takers.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:icn6y'
    female|a||Try one. Ana was not drawn, yet she is on Medicaid. Which kind of applicant is she?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:16ekd4p'
    'female|a||An always-taker: she is covered without a win, and with defiers ruled out, only always-takers are.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7720
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Now take Ben. He was drawn, and he is on Medicaid. Is he a complier?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||He could be either kind in the top row. Only his coverage had he lost would tell us, and that is the future nobody ever sees.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:119kcq3'
    female|a||So compliers can be counted to the percentage point, but not one of them can ever be named.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1qv06pa'
    female|a||Angrist, Imbens and Rubin set out these four kinds in 1996. What's left is to measure the compliers' effect without ever finding them.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:a7ctyk'
    'female|a||Now the money. Call spending out of pocket over six months Y: here is what each kind of applicant spends, drawn or not, in the same made-up numbers.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10200
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||Always-takers are covered either way, so the draw changes nothing for them: four hundred dollars, drawn or not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:z04pfg'
    'female|a||Never-takers are uncovered either way: a hundred dollars, drawn or not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:147gy65'
    'female|a||So winning does nothing for either group, and those zeros are an assumption with a name, exclusion: the letter may change spending only by changing coverage.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1xc9878'
    female|a||In Oregon it rules out, say, a winner who never enrols but stops worrying about bills, or books a check-up because the letter came.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1qatut0'
    'female|a||Compliers are covered only if drawn: a hundred and fifty dollars then, four hundred and fifty if not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:b6by40'
    female|a||So coverage saves each complier three hundred dollars, though no data set will ever show us this row.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:jt6fik'
    'female|a||What the data do show are the column averages across all hundred: a hundred and fifty-five dollars against two hundred and thirty-three.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1xb93p0'
    'female|a||Their gap, minus seventy-eight, comes entirely from the compliers'' row: twenty-six people saving three hundred each, spread across a hundred.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:kvoh51'
    'female|a||So divide the gap by the share who moved, the reduced form over the first stage: minus seventy-eight over zero point two six is minus three hundred, exactly the compliers'' saving.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1u8ndgo'
    'female|a||That ratio is the Wald estimator. In 1994, Imbens and Angrist showed what it measures under these assumptions: the average effect for compliers, the local average treatment effect.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:idrswo'
    'female|a||Each of the four assumptions holds up one piece of this table. Relevance: the draw must move someone, so the compliers'' share is not zero.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1916da7'
    'female|a||Independence: the draw is unrelated to each person''s potential coverage and potential spending, so the shares and the dollars are the same drawn or not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9yhy9r'
    female|a||Exclusion keeps those zeros at zero, and monotonicity keeps out a defier row that would pull the other way.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1mbhncm'
    female|a||Now break one. Suppose the letter itself got never-takers a free check-up, saving each of them $13. What would the Wald ratio now report?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ikx9yj'
    'female|a||Minus three hundred and thirty: the never-takers'' savings add about eight dollars to the gap, and dividing by 0.26 hands all of it to the compliers.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10840
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||That is what a broken exclusion looks like: the letter''s own effect on never-takers is credited to compliers, and the estimate grows by a tenth.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10120
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Now set the table aside and picture a weaker lottery, one that moves fewer people.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1itrzhe'
    'female|a||Watch the share fall toward zero: the gap shrinks, the answer stays, the error beside it grows.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1d6xbfk'
    female|a||As the share falls, the gap shrinks with it, and the ratio stays at minus three hundred.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||But a ten-dollar error in the gap becomes a hundred-dollar error when only one in ten moved, and a small breach of exclusion, like those thirteen dollars, is blown up the same way.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ddg1fm'
    female|a||Oregon's researchers ran essentially this division on real data, and their first-year mail survey shows it cleanly.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Only about half of those surveyed answered. Among them, about thirteen in a hundred not drawn were on Medicaid, and winning added twenty-nine points.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:fvzx9m'
    'female|a||Then one question: did you pay anything out of pocket for medical care in the last six months?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:sbx43v'
    'female|a||Among those not drawn, about fifty-six percent said yes. Among those drawn, it was almost six points fewer: the reduced form.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1er3hqv'
    female|a||Divide the one by the other, and coverage cut the share paying out of pocket by about twenty percentage points for compliers, give or take five.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9kir4z'
    female|a||About two years in, a second study examined some twelve thousand people around Portland. Coverage cut positive depression screens by about nine points from a base of thirty, though anything from two to seventeen fits the data.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 13720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:v5rjgm'
    female|a||But on blood pressure, cholesterol and blood sugar, it found no effect it could tell apart from zero.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ekp1ks'
    female|a||Some read that as coverage doing little for physical health in two years. Others answer that only about one in twenty had high blood sugar to begin with, too few to show even a sizeable improvement.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:36w5b8'
    female|a||What would tell them apart is a larger sample of people with diabetes, or a longer follow-up.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:hals2l'
    'female|a||Either way, every number here belongs to lottery compliers: the adults who would enrol only when drawn.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:hz7r69'
    'female|a||A new case. A clinic mails flu-shot reminders at random. Vaccinated: 50% with a reminder, 30% without. Caught flu: 9% against 10%. What does the Wald ratio say?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1wwqp3f'
    'female|a||Minus one point over twenty points of vaccination: five points less flu, for the people a reminder gets vaccinated, not for those who''d go anyway or never.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10320
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||So the gap between Oregon''s winners and losers was never the effect of Medicaid: it was that effect, carried by about a quarter of them and averaged over everyone.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Dividing by the first stage takes the dilution off, but only exclusion and monotonicity make that division honest.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1n1jv9r'
    'female|a||And the answer always belongs to someone: the people the instrument moved. Change the instrument, and you change who they are.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:157ac7f'
    'female|a||That is the bargain an instrument offers: a credible number, as long as you say whose it is.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1c9rwvz'
    'female|a||Look at the left column: who is on Medicaid without being drawn?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4920
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Yes.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 960
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Right.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1240
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||That's it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1040
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Exactly.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1360
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Spot on.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1160
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||You got it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1040
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Quite right.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1040
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Bang on.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1160
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||That's the one.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1280
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Indeed.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1040
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Yes — well done.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1520
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Nicely done.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1640
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Well done.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1480
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Lovely.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 920
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||The never-takers'' thirteen dollars now sit in the gap too: weight them by their sixty in a hundred, add, then divide.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Grab the share under the line and move it toward zero. Watch the gap above it, the answer, and the error on the right.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Divide the drop in flu by the rise in vaccination, then ask whose vaccination the letter changed.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
